    {
      "id": "claim_c2f786bc33d5426681f35264b0410b82",
      "statement": "Re-running the sorter against an already populated output tree is additive rather than idempotent: the input is copied again and normally receives a numeric suffix instead of updating the existing copy, and the application does not validate that output_path is separate from basepath, so an overlapping output location can add generated files beneath the source tree.",
